+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop on Quill Lane in Hollowmere. Plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript with no build step and no external requests.
+
+## Pages
+
+- `index.html`: home, with an introduction, featured books and the next upcoming events.
+- `books.html`: the catalogue of 14 titles across six genres, with a genre filter. The filter lives in the URL, for example `books.html?genre=mystery`.
+- `events.html`: upcoming and past events, split by the visitor's local date.
+- `visit.html`: opening hours, getting here, contact details and a contact form. The form is a demo and does not send anything.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `styles.css`: the shared stylesheet.
+- `js/books-data.js` and `js/events-data.js`: the data the pages read from. Edit these to change books or events.
+- `js/main.js`: the mobile navigation toggle, shared by every page.
+- `js/home.js`, `js/books.js`, `js/events.js`, `js/visit.js`: one script per page.
+- `tests/run.mjs`: headless browser tests. `tests/check-static.mjs`: static checks.
+
+## Running the site
+
+From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8000
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8000/. Opening `index.html` directly in a browser also works.
+
+## Running the tests
+
+The tests use Playwright and the system Chrome, which must be installed. Playwright is resolved from the environment and is not vendored here.
+
+```sh
+node tests/run.mjs            # all browser tests
+node tests/run.mjs books      # only tests whose name contains "books"
+node tests/check-static.mjs   # no external URLs, local references resolve, unique ids
+```
